# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored. See docs/self-hosting.md.

# The released image to run, with its version. Leave it out to run the image
# that `docker compose build` makes from this directory.
#APP_IMAGE=ghcr.io/wedsel2/garmin-analyzer:1.18.0

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Encrypts the stored Garmin tokens. Create one with:
#   docker compose run --rm web generate-key
# Keep it with your backups: without it every user has to link Garmin again.
# To replace it, put the new key first and the old one after a comma, run
# collect for every user, then remove the old key.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# How often the worker syncs each linked user, in minutes.
#SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60

# Where the web interface listens on the host. The default is this machine only;
# use 0.0.0.0:8000 to reach it from your network.
#WEB_BIND=127.0.0.1:8000

# Behind a reverse proxy or tunnel: the address the proxy connects from, so its
# forwarded headers are trusted. Without it the session cookie is not marked
# Secure and failed sign-ins of all users are counted together. Several
# addresses go after each other with commas, and a network such as
# 172.16.0.0/12 is allowed. The web service sees the address as Docker passes
# it on, which is often that of the Docker network and not of the proxy: when
# it is wrong, the log of the web service names the address to put here.
#FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=

# The coach: reports that Claude writes on a user's figures and goals. Each user
# turns it on for themselves; until then nothing of theirs leaves the instance.
# With a key here you pay for everyone, up to COACH_REPORTS_PER_DAY reports per
# user in 24 hours. Without one, a user can enter a key of their own, or take
# their figures as a text to a chat with Claude, which needs no key. Create a
# key at https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#COACH_REPORTS_PER_DAY=3
# The Claude model that writes; one of the Opus 5 or Sonnet 5 families.
#COACH_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
